Give a draft model's sliding-window KV layers a usable block size when their page does not
divide the primary page. Without this, a quantized KV cache costs a hybrid model with a
DFlash2 drafter MORE memory than bf16, not less.

`unify_kv_cache_spec_page_size` equalizes page sizes by scaling a layer's block size up by
the integer ratio max_page / own_page, and falls back to padding the *page* when that ratio
is not an integer. Sliding-window layers are born at the backend's smallest kernel block --
16 -- because the code that picks it assumes unify will scale it (the comment at
model_executor/layers/attention/attention.py reads "the smallest block is fine -- `unify`
scales it up by an integer ratio"). When the ratio is not an integer, that assumption fails
silently: the block stays 16 and every block pays a whole primary page.

On this repo's target + DFlash2 drafter the divisibility holds at bf16 only by coincidence.
The target has 4 KV heads x 256 head dim and the drafter 8 x 128, so both need 4096 B per
token per layer and the ratio is exactly 28. A per-token-head quantized cache adds one fp32
scale *per head*, which breaks it: 2*4*(256+4) = 2080 for the target against 2*8*(128+4) =
2112 for the drafter, and 2112 = 2**6 * 3 * 11 shares no useful factor with the primary page,
so no block size ever divides it. The drafter's 5 layers then took
cdiv(2047 + 4096, 16) + 1 = 385 blocks of 1.71 MiB each -- 1.88% utilised, a constant
5.155 GiB, 75.6% of the whole per-request budget. Measured: int8 needed 6.82 GiB to serve
32,768 tokens where bf16 serves 69,758 in 5.2 GiB.

The fix rounds such a layer's block size *up* to the smallest multiple of its own kernel
granularity whose natural page covers the maximum, and lets that page become the new maximum
so every other layer pads up by a percent or two instead. Those layers hold hundreds of
blocks each, so paying 1.5% on them is far cheaper than 385 nearly-empty pages on the drafter.
Guarded: it only fires when every other spec can actually accept padding (Mamba by
construction, attention only if its backend indexes KV by block stride), so it never turns a
configuration that starts today into a NotImplementedError.

Measured on the 3090, SPEC=dflash2 DFLASH_TOKENS=7, --kv-cache-memory=5583457484:

  int8_per_token_head, estimated max model length   3,536 -> 94,176
  int8_per_token_head pool at max_model_len 131,072  would not start -> 138,696 tokens
  bf16 (block size / needed / estimated max)         448 / 16.88 GiB / 46,592, unchanged,
                                                     and zero promotions logged

138,696 against bf16's 69,758 is 1.99x the context in the same pool. bf16 is untouched
because its pages already divide.

The promoted block must also DIVIDE the primary block (#63). Covering the maximum page is
only half the requirement: the scheduler's granularity is the LCM of the primary groups'
blocks, and kv_cache_coordinator asserts that every group's block divides it. The first
version of this patch only made the page cover, and got away with it at DFLASH_TOKENS=7
by luck -- the drafter landed on 848 against a primary block of 1696, exactly half. The
mamba page grows with the spec-decode state, so at DFLASH_TOKENS=15 the primary block
moves 1696 -> 1840 while the drafter's covering block is 928, which divides nothing the
scheduler can use, and the engine died in a bare `assert` three layers down. So round the
promotion up to the smallest divisor of the primary block that still covers, and bail out
(back to the expensive-but-working padding) if there is none.

Measured on the 3090, alternative.sh (int4_per_token_head), MAX_LEN=32768:

  DFLASH_TOKENS=7   1696 / 848  scheduler 1696, unchanged by this fix, pool 142,843 tokens
  DFLASH_TOKENS=15  1840 / 928  AssertionError in kv_cache_coordinator.py -> boots:
                    drafter 16 -> 1840, primary scales 1840 -> 3680, pool 53,908 tokens

At 15 the whole 256k default no longer fits (estimated maximum model length 180,320), which
is the documented cost of a wider verify block, not a new failure. CTX=huge (KVarN) at
DFLASH_TOKENS=15 is untouched: 228,296 tokens, same as before.

Apply from the repo root, after hybrid-kv-groups-v2-cudagraph.patch:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/hybrid-sw-block-promote.patch

Validated against vLLM 0.28.0. Reapply after upgrades.

